    [
      "nested_1",
      "Nested BEJSON (Elton's proposed pattern -- NOT finalized, treat as under consideration, not settled spec): a field's Values cell in a 104 file can itself hold another full 104 document (its own Fields + Values), recursively, to declare hierarchical/relational data inside ONE file. No format change -- 104 itself doesn't change, this just permits an embedded 104 document as a cell's value and recurses into it as a parent-child relationship, where the parent cell is the implicit foreign key. E.g. a top-level 'users' field whose cells are each a full per-user 104 file, which could itself have an 'rpg_stats' field whose cells are a third-tier nested 104 -- unlimited depth. OPEN QUESTION Elton flagged and has NOT decided: should every nested record at a given tier (e.g. every user) share one common field schema, or can each have custom fields? His own lean is 'shared schema for all' to avoid bottlenecks, but he explicitly said this isn't settled -- ask him if it matters for the task at hand rather than assuming either answer.",
      "keyword_only",
      true,
      2
