    [
      "diagrams_1",
      "Diagrams family (lib_bejson_Diagrams_diagrams_core.py): write-path library owning the Board/Connector/Territory MFDB entity schema used by diagram apps. Key functions: diagrams_core_create_database(root_dir, db_name, ...) creates a diagram's MFDB root; diagrams_core_export_package(mfdb_root_dir, db_name, ...) and diagrams_core_write_package_file(...) package it as ONE portable .mfdb132.bejson document (MFDB 1.32 chunk/unchunk style) instead of a zipped 1.31 MFDB directory -- 1.31 zip export is still valid for non-diagram MFDB apps, diagrams specifically standardize on 1.32 because a diagram is meant to end up as one file; diagrams_core_import_package_file(src_path, output_dir, ...) reverses that; diagrams_core_find_row_by_field(doc, field_name, value) looks up a row by field value.",
