      "behtml_lib_1",
      "BEHTML library (lib_bejson_BEHTML_core.py): pure functions implementing the spec's spatial math, no Flask/I/O. Key calls: behtml_core_quantize_y(height_px) / behtml_core_y_span_to_px(y_span) convert between raw pixels and the Ry=32px quantum; behtml_core_validate_quantization(actual_px, y_span, ...) is the Anti-Drift Auditor's tolerance check; behtml_core_control_padding_y(...) derives the symmetrical padding for the 28px-paradox controls; behtml_core_validate_x_address(x_start, x_span) / behtml_core_x_span_to_percent(...) / behtml_core_percent_to_x_span(...) handle the 8-lane X-axis math; behtml_core_bem_class(block, element, modifier) / behtml_core_grid_cell_classes(...) build the behtml- BEM class strings; behtml_core_validate_contrast(font_color, background_color) enforces the tri-color contrast laws.",
